context-deny: [a-z0-9](File|Path|Dir|Url|Uri|Name|Id|Env|Var|Hash|Digest|Regex|Pattern|Policy|Length|Min|Max|Enabled|Disabled|Required|Optional|Field|Header|Param|Prompt|Label|Title|Text|Message|Type|Format|Ttl|Expiry|Expires|Rotation|Suffix|Prefix|Count|Size|Limit|Algo|Algorithm|Encoding|Mask|Hint|Reset|Confirm|Attempts|Lockout|Column|Table|Schema|Version|Strength|Score|Age|History)["'`]?[[:space:]]*[:=]
# UNQUOTED-ONLY precision guard: a bare value made only of lowercase letters
# joined by . _ - or / is an identifier, a slug, a dotted name or a relative
# path, not a credential - `local secretsset=sast_hist_secrets` and
# `secret-file: relative/path` are both real matches this rule made against
# scoursh's own tree.  Deliberately NOT applied to the quoted records above:
# quoting is itself an authoring signal, and `password: "correct-horse"` is a
# real password shape.  The accepted cost is stated in the header matrix: an
# unquoted all-lowercase hyphen/underscore password is not reported here.
context-deny: [:=][[:space:]]*[a-z]{1,40}[._/-][a-z._/-]{1,60}([[:space:]]|$)
context-window: 0
tags: static
remediation: Remove the literal credential from the assignment and rotate it.
  Supply it at runtime from the environment or a secret store; a value committed in a
  .env file, a Dockerfile ENV, or a CI configuration is committed in git history.
references: CWE-798

id: SAST-SEC-JWT-01
title: Hardcoded JSON Web Token
severity: high
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-798
owasp: A07:2025
pattern: eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{5,}\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{5,}\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{5,}
dialect: ere
tags: static
remediation: Remove the token from source; a hardcoded JWT is a long-lived bearer credential
  and must be treated as compromised once committed.
  Mint tokens at runtime through the normal authentication flow instead.
references: CWE-798
